            "review_title": "Review at Pho Container",
            "review_text": "Yogaholi_ca\nHong Kong, China7 contributions\n0\nHow did it get such good review??\nNov 2018 • Solo\nFirst of all, this place was owned by Korean. Maybe so, there were a lot of Korean customers. Perhaps the cook is Vietnamese but I didn’t feel it authentic at all. It’s pricey yet taste worse than some cheap & small noodles shop.\nI ordered the basic beef noodle soup and fried spring roll. \nThe noodle bowl was quite small, the soup was too sweet with strong black pepper taste and no Beef stock taste. The beef was not tender, it took me some time to chew. And the spring roll was wrapped with curd skin (not spring roll wrap) and it was not crunchy. Again it was hard to chew while it was frying hot in my mouth...imagine~~!!\n\nOverall, it was total disappointment.\nRead more\nWritten November 27, 2018",
