            "review_text": "Joanne Kwok\nHong Kong, China207 contributions\n8\nTasty Pho\nNov 2017 • Friends\nThis small pho place is in an alley and a bit difficult to notice it on the street and you might expect that it is kind of mom and pop place. When we entered the restaurant, we find the interior is quite chic and trendy. We are impressed. \n\nMenu is small and we ordered pho (beef noodle soup), fried seafood rice paper roll and spring roll. The pho is tasty and rice paper roll is good too. But the spring roll is a bit over cooked. \n\nIn general, food and service is good and price is reasonable. Try this place if you come by this neighbourhood.\nRead more\nWritten January 22, 2018",
